  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 447.84pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 468.72pt, "Future long-duration space missions will require in-situ, on-demand manufacturing of tools and components. ")
  #line-at(54pt, 483.301pt, "Photopolymer-based processes are attractive for this purpose due to their low energy requirements, volume ")
  #line-at(54pt, 497.817pt, "efficiency, and precise control of curing. However, photopolymerization generates significant heat, which is difficult ")
  #line-at(54pt, 512.398pt, "to regulate in microgravity where natural convection is absent, leading to defects such as surface blistering and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 526.914pt, "deformation. In this work, we combine experimental studies and modeling to address these thermal challenges. We ")
  #line-at(54pt, 541.495pt, "report results from International Space Station (ISS) experiments and a dedicated parabolic flight campaign, which ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 556.011pt, "confirm that suppressed convective heat transfer in microgravity exacerbates thermal buildup and defect formation. ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 570.592pt, "Building on these observations, we present a predictive thermal model that couples heat transfer, light absorption, ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 585.108pt, "and evolving material properties to simulate polymerization and temperature evolution under terrestrial and ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 599.624pt, "microgravity conditions. Laboratory validation demonstrates strong agreement between model predictions and ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 614.205pt, "measured temperature profiles. Applying the model to the ISS experiments, we show that the model accurately ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 628.721pt, "reproduces experimentally observed blistering in TJ-3704A, a commercial acrylate-based polymer resin, while also ")
  #line-at(53.967pt, 643.302pt, "predicting defect-free outcomes for Norland optical adhesives. The model functions as a design tool for defect-free ")
  #line-at(53.967pt, 657.818pt, "in-space manufacturing, enabling selection of polymer properties, exposure strategies, and environmental conditions ")
  #line-at(53.967pt, 672.399pt, "that together inhibit excess thermal buildup, paving the way for scalable, reliable in-situ manufacturing during future ")
  #line-at(53.978pt, 686.915pt, "missions. ")
]

