#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 758.76pt, "Page 2 of 18 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 83.22pt, "Keywords ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 104.1pt, "In-space manufacturing (ISM), photopolymerization, microgravity, Fluidic Shaping, photopolymer optics, thermal ")
  #line-at(54pt, 118.681pt, "blistering, in-space lens fabrication, thermal model. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 140.16pt, "1.")
  #line-at(72pt, 140.16pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 161.1pt, "The most significant human presence in space to date is the International Space Station (ISS), located just 400 ")
  #line-at(54pt, 175.616pt, "kilometers above Earth. While 13 metric tons of spares are stored on board, the logistics model for its operation still ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 190.197pt, "requires more than 3 metric tons of resupply from Earth each year. It is clear that for future long-duration missions, ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 204.713pt, "such as crewed Mars expeditions, where resupply from Earth is unavailable, a fundamental shift in mission planning ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 219.294pt, "is essential. Such missions will need to be able to manufacture tools, replacement parts, and functional components ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 233.875pt, "in-space and on-demand")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(161.52pt, 229.86pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(165pt, 233.88pt, ".  ")
  #line-at(53.992pt, 255.236pt, "Since 2011, NASA’s In Space Manufacturing project (ISM) has been actively developing capabilities for on-")
  #line-at(53.981pt, 269.818pt, "demand in-space manufacturing and repair. Numerous approaches for in-space manufacturing have been pursued. ")
  #line-at(53.981pt, 284.333pt, "The majority of methods are based on polymer additive-manufacturing such as FDM 3D-printing (e.g. Made In ")
  #line-at(53.981pt, 298.915pt, "Space’s 3DP and AMF projects, Tethers Unlimited Inc. Refabricator), direct robotic extrusion of photopolymers ")
  #line-at(53.981pt, 313.496pt, "(DREPP")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(91.86pt, 309.48pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.34pt, 313.5pt, "), selective UV exposure of photopolymers (VAM: SpaceCAL")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(372.3pt, 309.48pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(375.78pt, 313.5pt, ", DLP: Auxilium Biotechnologies’ AMP-")
  #line-at(54pt, 328.982pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(59.52pt, 324.96pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(63pt, 328.98pt, ", LCD: Photocentric’s CosmicMaker")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(224.82pt, 324.96pt, "5")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(228.36pt, 328.98pt, "), and our own approach, Fluidic")
  #line-at(374.504pt, 328.98pt, "Shaping")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(410.58pt, 324.96pt, "6,7")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(419.4pt, 328.98pt, ". ")
  #line-at(53.997pt, 350.336pt, "Photopolymers are particularly attractive for space as they require a very small energy budget and infrastructure in ")
  #line-at(53.997pt, 364.852pt, "comparison to other materials. They allow precise control of polymerization initiation and location, while ")
  #line-at(53.997pt, 379.433pt, "eliminating the need for extensive heating of feed material or for on-site homogeneous and bubble-free mixing of ")
  #line-at(53.986pt, 393.949pt, "multi-component resins. Despite this mechanical simplification, the thermodynamics of polymerization remains a ")
  #line-at(53.986pt, 408.53pt, "challenge. The photopolymerization reaction is inherently exothermic, releasing significant heat that, if unaccounted ")
  #line-at(53.975pt, 423.046pt, "for, may undermine successful fabrication. At high temperatures, photopolymer resins are prone to evaporation of ")
  #line-at(53.975pt, 437.627pt, "volatiles, surface deformations, and blistering (see Supplementary Video 3), and in extreme cases, loss of chemical ")
  #line-at(53.964pt, 452.209pt, "stability")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(89.46pt, 448.2pt, "8")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(92.94pt, 452.22pt, ". These challenges exist in terrestrial fabrication but are exacerbated in space where temperature regulation ")
  #line-at(54.005pt, 467.581pt, "is hindered by the absence of free convection, and even more so in large structures, where the surface area to volume ")
  #line-at(54.005pt, 482.162pt, "ratio diminishes. ")
  #line-at(54.005pt, 502.684pt, "As shown in Figure 1, during our 2022 ISS experiment (see Supplementary Video 1), we observed firsthand the ")
  #line-at(54.016pt, 517.266pt, "detrimental effects of microgravity on photopolymer based fabrication.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(378.42pt, 512.76pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(381.96pt, 517.26pt, " As part of the RAKIA Ax-1 mission, ")
  #line-at(53.998pt, 531.776pt, "astronaut Eytan Stibbe demonstrated in-space manufacturing of optical lenses using our Fluidic Shaping method ")
  #line-at(53.987pt, 546.357pt, "(Figure1A-B). Fluidic Shaping exploits the dominancy of surface-tension in the microgravity environment to ")
  #line-at(53.987pt, 560.873pt, "naturally shape liquid polymer resins into smooth spherical lenses, which are then solidified by polymerization.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(555.6pt, 556.38pt, "6")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54.005pt, 575.396pt, "During the experiment, we used three different photopolymers: TJ-3704A, a commercial acrylate-based resin also ")
  #line-at(54.027pt, 589.977pt, "sold under the brand name ‘VidaRosa’ (Dongguan Tianxingjian Electronic Technology Co., Ltd, Guandong, China), ")
  #line-at(54.038pt, 604.493pt, "and NOA61 & NOA63 (Norland Optical Adhesive, Norland Products Incorporated, New Jersey, USA). In ground-")
  #line-at(54.038pt, 619.074pt, "based tests, we produced high-quality optics using all these materials (Figure 1D), yet to our surprise, during the ")
  #line-at(54.016pt, 633.59pt, "ISS experiment, the lenses made from the TJ-3704A exhibited severe blistering on their free surface (Figure 1C) – ")
  #line-at(54.016pt, 648.171pt, "a phenomenon we had not observed until then. This was further accompanied by deformations of the plastic frames ")
  #line-at(54.005pt, 662.687pt, "and noticeable release of fumes (see Supplementary Video 2).")
  #line-at(54pt, 683.22pt, "We hypothesize that the unexpected behavior of TJ-3704A is the result of extreme thermal build-up during ")
  #line-at(54pt, 697.801pt, "polymerization, caused by the absence of natural convection in microgravity.  This suggests that understanding and ")
  #line-at(53.989pt, 712.317pt, "predicting the temperature distribution and propagation during the fabrication process is crucial to successful ")
]

